.TH UWCC-MODELS 1 "October 2026" "UWCC 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uwcc-models \- download and prepare local UWCC models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uwcc-models
.RI { prepare | prepare-gpu | validate-gpu }
.RI [ --models-dir " DIRECTORY" ]
.RI [ --download-only ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download pinned weights from their original upstream hosts, verify checksums,
and convert them to ONNX. Run as your desktop user, without sudo.
No models are downloaded during Debian package installation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B prepare
Download UDnet and FastDVDnet sources and weights, convert models, and validate
inference parity using CPU PyTorch and ONNX.
.TP
.B prepare-gpu
Prepare dynamic FP32/FP16 FastDVDnet graphs from previously downloaded weights.
.TP
.B validate-gpu
Validate and register the GPU variants. Requires an active CUDA runtime;
use uwcc-nvidia model-tools validate-gpu after NVIDIA setup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --models-dir DIRECTORY
Use the selected directory instead of UWCC_MODEL_DIR or the default
$XDG_DATA_HOME/uwcc/models (normally ~/.local/share/uwcc/models).
.TP
.B --download-only
Download sources and weights without conversion. Only valid with prepare.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uwcc (1),
.BR uwcc-nvidia (1)
